=== Climate ===
Shiga Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate (Köppen ''Am''), moderated by the maritime influence of the Katsuran Sea. The western coast experiences warm, humid conditions year-round with a pronounced wet season from May through October, when the Shendan monsoon drives moist air across the Katsuran Sea and into the Ishijima interior. The Katsuran Sea's relatively stable water temperatures create a moderating effect on the coastal climate, reducing the diurnal temperature variation compared to the interior prefectures.

The Shiga Hills create a partial rain shadow for the eastern highlands, which receive less precipitation than the coast. The coastal industrial corridor, exposed to the full force of the Katsuran Sea weather systems, receives the heaviest rainfall and the most frequent typhoon impacts of any inland-sea coast on Ishijima.

